WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:02.900
Hello, I’m Robert Schaub.

2
00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:06.550
Facts and evidence
are an essential foundation

3
00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:11.620
for democracy, justice
and good business decisions.

4
00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:15.100
I’m working on Evidence-Gated Agents.

5
00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.990
Before AI acts, it must have permission

6
00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:22.020
and enough evidence
to justify the action.

7
00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:27.880
I spent 39 years in software engineering
and project leadership.

8
00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:32.500
I founded FactHarbor,
a Swiss non-profit association.

9
00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.000
I’ve built two separate projects:

10
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.960
the FactHarbor fact-checking application.

11
00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:43.200
It assesses claims against
supporting and opposing evidence.

12
00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:48.600
And Our AI Charter Runtime,
an early prototype.

13
00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:52.820
It checks permission and evidence
before allowing an AI action.

14
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:57.610
With funding, I will be able to build
and test a working

15
00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:01.980
Evidence-Gated Agents prototype
using these two foundations.

16
00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:04.820
Here is a practical example:

17
00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.200
replacing oil heating
with an air-to-water heat pump.

18
00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:12.710
Can this be generally recommended

19
00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:15.800
without first checking
the building’s specific conditions?

20
00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:20.360
This FactHarbor report
weighs the evidence.

21
00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.600
Here you can inspect
the evidence and its source.

22
00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:31.530
Now, in the Evidence-Gated Agents
prototype,

23
00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:35.050
a user submits a question or claim.

24
00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:39.890
The AI drafts an answer
using evidence from FactHarbor reports.

25
00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:44.220
A separate gateway will check
current authority and evidence

26
00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:46.670
for that exact answer.

27
00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:49.980
The gateway can allow or block the answer,

28
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.870
or ask a human reviewer
to narrow or decline the request.

29
00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:58.770
Every revision must pass all checks again.

30
00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:03.680
If the answer is released,
it comes with a receipt you can inspect.

31
00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:07.450
It links the answer, authority, evidence,

32
00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:09.970
reasoning, decision and outcome.

33
00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:14.460
Beyond the prototype, I want to develop

34
00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:18.690
evidence-gated decision-making
applications and services.

35
00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:23.220
With permission, a future product
could also gather and use

36
00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:26.210
an organisation’s non-public evidence.

37
00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:28.620
Consequential AI-based decisions

38
00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:32.190
must always be open
to inspection and challenge.

39
00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:36.580
I want to work with the Prototype Fund’s
coaches and participants

40
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:40.810
to challenge my assumptions
and develop the project further.

41
00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.020
Through its network, I’d like to involve

42
00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.030
potential users in testing the prototype.

43
00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:50.460
My vision is a free and fair society

44
00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.390
where consequential decisions
must remain authorised,

45
00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:57.630
grounded in evidence
and open to challenge.
